  "drivers": [
    {
      "text": "Iran's nuclear programme has been disputed for two decades: the 2015 deal that limited it lost force after the US left it in 2018, and Iran then enriched uranium beyond the deal's limits.",
      "source": {
        "name": "Council on Foreign Relations",
        "url": "https://www.cfr.org/backgrounder/what-iran-nuclear-deal"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Iran has long backed armed groups across the region, including Hezbollah, Hamas, the Houthis and Iraqi militias; the US and Israel cite that network and the nuclear programme as threats.",
      "source": {
        "name": "Council on Foreign Relations",
        "url": "https://www.cfr.org/global-conflict-tracker/conflict/confrontation-between-united-states-and-iran"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The Gaza war that followed the Hamas-led attack on Israel on 7 October 2023 spread across the region: Hezbollah, the Houthis and Iraqi armed groups joined in, and Israel and Iran fought a twelve-day war in June 2025.",
      "source": {
        "name": "Council on Foreign Relations",
        "url": "https://www.cfr.org/global-conflict-tracker/conflict/israeli-palestinian-conflict"
      }
    }
  ],
